{{rfc|date=July 2005}}
==English==

===Interjection===
'''ohi'''

# A casual greeting exchanged between former players of Quake and EverQuest. When coupled with "pal", it is indicative of friendly intent on the part of the speaker.

----

==Finnish==

===Adverb===
{{infl|fi|adverb}}

# (''temporal'') [[over]]
#:*Se on '''ohi''' nyt.
#:**It is ''over'' now.

===Postposition===
{{infl|fi|postposition|+ [[genitive]]}}

# [[by]], [[past]] (when one goes ''through'' the space that is ''next to'' something):
#:*Pallo pyöri tuolin '''ohi''' ja ovesta ulos.
#:**The ball rolled ''by'' the chair and out of the door.
# (''spatial'') [[wide]] 
#*''Nuoli meni maalin '''ohi'''.''
#**The arrow fell ''wide'' of the mark.

===Preposition===
([[elative]] +) {{infl|fi|preposition}}

# (''spatial'') [[past]]
#*''Olimme jo '''ohi''' sillasta, kun onnettomuus tapahtui.''
#**We were already ''past'' the bridge, when the accident took place.

